\1 {iconscript} {iconscript}

iconscript is a language for describing pixel-wise pictograms in the style of
the \ref {https://github.com/enzet/Roentgen} {Röntgen} project.

The grammar of the language is described in the ANTLR4
\c {grammar/IconScript.g4} file.

\2 {SVG generation} {svg-generation}

There are two implementations of iconscript for parsing and generating SVG
files.
\list
    {
        \s {Rust}: \c {cargo install iconscript}. Rust implementation is
        \e {faster} and \e {more reliable}. It uses
        \ref
            {https://docs.rs/linesweeper/latest/linesweeper/} {\c {linesweeper}}
        library for Boolean path operations and SVG optimizations.
    }
    {
        \s {JavaScript} (TypeScript): \c {npm install iconscript}. JavaScript
        implementation uses \ref {http://paperjs.org/} {Paper.js} library, that
        may produce wrong outputs.
    }

